From b008c2067ade19eaad3a0a6663457dededea7c86 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew de los Reyes <adlr@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Nov 2025 11:14:57 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 10/24] TILETEAR: CrtcFrame.crtc->crtcs

Also, CrtcFrame.submitted_update.latch_crtc->latch_crtcs

Also, MetaKmsImplDevice: ensure_crtc_frame ensures only one CrtcFrame per Crtc

Crtcs can be reused as monitor configurations change. For example, a
Crtc may be be part of a tiled monitor group, or it may be driving a
laptop internal display. This same Crtc may serve both functions
depending on how a monitor configuration changes over time.

ensure_crtc_frame is trying to find the CrtcFrame for a set of Crtcs.
If it can't find the exact set already existing, it frees the old
CrtcFrames and creates a new one for the new set.
