From c4c12bab276c899eddc538525f01a062add02b10 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew de los Reyes <adlr@chromium.org>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 09:40:13 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 14/24] TILETEAR: Create MetaRendererViews from a
 MetaRenderTarget

MetaLogicalMonitor now builds a MetaRenderTarget for each group of
CRTCs and hands that to MetaRenderer::create_view(), which passes it on
to MetaOnscreenNative, instead of passing a bare (MetaOutput, MetaCrtc)
pair down the chain. The render target owns the refs and the view takes
its own, so meta_renderer_native_create_view() no longer leaks one.

The onscreen is now sized with meta_render_target_get_output_frame()
and the view laid out with meta_render_target_get_view_layout().

No functional change: meta_logical_monitor_foreach_crtc() still walks
one CRTC at a time, so every render target holds exactly one CRTC and
output, for which both of those return what the CRTC config said before.
